  "body_excerpt": "<p>In Splunk AI Toolkit versions below 5.7.4, a user who holds the “admin” Splunk role could execute arbitrary OS commands on the host running the Splunk Enterprise instance.</p>\n\n<p>The vulnerability is possible because of an unsafe shell execution pattern in the btool configuration helper, which constructs OS command strings from dynamic parameters without disabling shell interpretation.</p>",
